**Short answer:** Lemonade's FY2024 results landed at or above the top of the full-year guidance it gave in its prior-quarter (Q3 2024) report. In-force premium hit the top of the range, revenue beat it, and Adjusted EBITDA loss came in better than the range.

**Prior-quarter guidance (Q3 2024 report, Oct 30, 2024):** <cite index="11-10">Lemonade increased full year guidance for gross earned premium and revenue, and reaffirmed guidance for FY 2024 for all other metrics.</cite> The Q3 full-year ranges were: in-force premium $940–$944M, gross earned premium $823–$826M, revenue $522–$524M, and Adjusted EBITDA loss of ($155)–($151)M (per the <cite index="4-2">Q4 2024 and full-year 2024 guidance table</cite>).

**FY2024 actuals vs. guidance:**

1. **In-force premium (IFP):** Actual was $944M against a $940–$944M range, so it landed at the top end. Management said it <cite index="22-17">delivered on that guidance with notable precision, ending 2024 with IFP of $944 million, representing 26% year on year growth</cite>.

2. **Revenue:** Actual full-year total revenue was $526.5M, <cite index="28-1">an increase of 22% (from prior year)</cite>. This is above the $522–$524M range, about $2.5M above the top end and $3.5M above the midpoint (+0.67%). The quarterly figures support this total: Q1 $119.1M, Q2 $122.0M, Q3 $136.6M and Q4 $148.8M, which sum to $526.5M. Q4 revenue beat expectations as well; <cite index="8-5">revenue of $148.8 million, a 29% increase year-over-year, surpassed analyst expectations of $144.9 million.</cite>

3. **Gross earned premium (GEP):** The company did not state a full-year GEP total in the sources I found. Summing the quarterly figures (Q1 $187.9M, Q2 $199.9M, Q3 $213.1M, and Q4 about $226M, which is a rounded figure from the earnings call) gives roughly $826.9M. That is slightly above the $823–$826M range, but the result is approximate because Q4 is rounded.

4. **Adjusted EBITDA:** Actual full-year Adjusted EBITDA loss was ($150)M, against guidance of ($155)–($151)M. That is about $1M better than the best end of the range and about $3M better than the midpoint of ($153)M (roughly a 2% smaller loss). Management <cite index="22-18">reported an Adj. EBITDA loss of ($150) million, 13% year on year improvement.</cite>

**Conclusion:** Against the prior-quarter full-year guidance, Lemonade met or beat every metric. IFP was at the top of its range, revenue (~$526.5M) exceeded its range, GEP was at or slightly above the top (approximate), and the Adjusted EBITDA loss was smaller than guided.

Sources:
- Q3 2024 shareholder letter (8-K): guidance and Q3 results
- Q4 2024 shareholder letter (8-K): FY2024 IFP and Adjusted EBITDA results
- Q1 2024, Q2 2024 shareholder letters (8-K): quarterly revenue and GEP
- Q4 2024 earnings call transcript (Motley Fool): Q4 GEP and revenue
- Crowdfund Insider: Q4 revenue vs. analyst expectations
- Lemonade 2025 proxy statement (DEF 14A): full-year total revenue

